	quest.008C70AC22DA5527.title: "Wires"
	quest.01F18150EC923482.quest_desc: [
		"&9Refined Storage&r is a mass storage mod that offers a network-based storage system."
		""
		"To get started with the mod, you'll want to make the &9Controller&r."
		""
		"The Controller is the \"Core\" of your storage network. When provided with power, it gives life to all RS components connected. Each network can only have one Controller."
	]
	quest.01F18150EC923482.title: "Refined Storage"
	quest.01FDC26D065C585E.quest_desc: ["In this pack, Stone Tools are crafted with Flint."]
	quest.01FDC26D065C585E.title: "Stone Tools"
	quest.05A8535BB4A1F5D3.title: "Upgrades"
	quest.0684261C4BC17C77.quest_desc: ["Deployers unlock many new automation possibilities, such as wool, milk and tree farms."]
	quest.0684261C4BC17C77.title: "Deployer"
	quest.08E5994F6BFB4B72.quest_desc: ["Four new crops can be found in the wild or in chests. These will prove essential to cook the most nutricious meals."]
	quest.08E5994F6BFB4B72.title: "Crops of the Wild"
	quest.09CFAA082C8B65D5.quest_desc: [
		"In this modpack, the vanilla hunger system is disabled."
		""
		"Instead, you have &93 food slots&r that you must fill by eating."
		""
		"Each food slot filled gives you &cextra hearts&r and better regeneration, until the food runs out."
		""
		"Food's bonuses and duration are visible on its tooltip. The more nutritious the food, the better the effects."
	]
	quest.09CFAA082C8B65D5.title: "Health and Hunger System"
	quest.0CAB43281108C554.title: "Villager in a Box"
	quest.0CD4F1D4BC3FE4AD.title: "\"We're in the End Game now.\""
	quest.0D24CE4CFE861457.quest_desc: [
		"Several resources have been made renewable in this pack. Below a couple examples you might want to automate:"
		""
		"-&3Tuff&r &7&o(mixing Cobblestone + Water)&r&r"
		"-&3Soul Soil&r &7&o(haunting Sand blocks)&r&r"
		"-&3Limestone &r&7&o(Lava + Honey generator)&r&r"
		"-&3Scoria &r&7&o(Lava + Chocolate generator)&r&r"
		"-&3Basalt &r&7&o(Lava + Blue Ice generator, with a Soul Soil block under the empty space)&r&r"
	]
	quest.0D24CE4CFE861457.title: "Late Game Automation"
	quest.0F865DD230781FA8.title: "Create: Winery"
	quest.10191888E8E7FABD.quest_desc: [
		"This modpack is a &6Create&r centric pack, full of custom content. Many vanilla and modded recipes have been modified for a smooth progression."
		""
		"The &oATM9-style&r quest book is divised into several chapters, each with their own questline to give you milestones to reach."
		""
		"The first and last quests of each chapter are marked by a book icon:"
		""
		"{image:ftbquests:textures/gui/guide.png width:25 height:25 align:1}"
		""
		"I tried to keep this pack lightweight and focused, yet still having all the necessary machines and tools to build complex contraptions. Have fun!"
	]
	quest.10191888E8E7FABD.title: "Welcome to Create: Gears of History!"
	quest.10C93E580AA3689F.title: "Molten Copper"
	quest.12A43F82FC67A289.quest_desc: [
		"To store your items, you'll need to create disks that are stored in a &9Disk Drive&r. You can attach this to your network by placing it beside your Controller, or by using pipes. These have 8 slots for Storage Drives."
		""
		"Please note that for bulk storage, it's wiser to use your Refined Storage Disks in combination with Drawers. This way you will save a lot of space in the Disks (having 10,000 Cobblestone on a Disk is a waste of disk space)."
		""
		"Once you have your Disk Drive, it's time to create the \"Hard Drives\" of Refined Storage. To do this, we'll need a &9Storage Housing&r that we'll combine with a &9Storage Part&r to create a &9Storage Disk&r. Just simply make the desired size of part, then combine with the housing to create a disk."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The Storage Disk is used to store your items virtually once placed inside of the Disk Drive. It has to be put in a Disk Drive. The Storage Disk won’t despawn when dropped in the world."
		""
		"&l&nIMPORTANT&r: Do not store NBT items on a disk. This increases overall lag in the chunk, and &lcan eventually corrupt your save&r. If you are unsure what NBT items are, the general rule of thumb is \"If it doesn't stack, don't put it in your system.\""
		""
		"NBT items are regular items that have tags attached to them, like durability of items, enchantments, flag colors, etc. You know those Chestplates you keep getting from killing mobs? Those enchanted pickaxes? Yea, don't put that in your Refined Storage system."
	]
	quest.12A43F82FC67A289.title: "Creating Virtual Storage"
	quest.13152EF9BE7618EB.quest_desc: ["When powered with Stress units it will generate FE Power."]
	quest.14B99B3C6C034C8C.quest_desc: ["Fans can be used very early game for bulk smelting."]
	quest.14E8C6AF337618DA.quest_desc: ["In this pack, you don't need an anvil to rename a nametag, you can do it by simply sneak + right-clicking on the item. Renaming items won't cost you any experience points!"]
	quest.14E8C6AF337618DA.title: "Free Renames"
	quest.15AFB741027D374D.title: "Steel Alloy"
	quest.16EAB47A928B52C0.title: "Iron Armor"
	quest.18839505B9993252.title: "Create: Aeronautics"
	quest.1A2DF45C2673741A.title: "Sturdy Sheet"
	quest.1AA9FE35ED67B2E1.quest_desc: ["Congratulations for making it this far!"]
	quest.1AA9FE35ED67B2E1.title: "A strange material..."
	quest.1B4B24EA93D908F3.title: "Create: Wrapped"
	quest.1D87243244A0142A.title: "Storage"
	quest.1F2C1E293141CF3C.title: "Chainmail Armor"
	quest.221AAB63F61099CF.title: "Andesite Alloy Ingredients"
	quest.22A2B5C8C025849B.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations, you've made it to the end and completed the modpack! I hope you enjoyed it."
		""
		"If you're a content creator and you made videos about this modpack, feel free to send me a message, I'll be glad to feature your videos on the project page!"
		""
		"Thank you for playing! &7-robinfrt&r"
		""
		"{image:minecraft:textures/mob_effect/health_boost.png width:10 height:10 align:1}"
	]
	quest.22A2B5C8C025849B.title: "Going Creative"
	quest.269E990F84155E67.quest_desc: ["This is certainly a bit overkill..."]
	quest.2A9ABB7C959C665C.quest_subtitle: "{count:1,id:\"refinedstorage:1024b_fluid_storage_block\"}"
	quest.2B27E4E04A628C60.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Speed Upgrade&r does exactly what it says it does. It will increase the speed at which the interface/block works. Need an importer to pull faster? Want your crafters to work faster? This is the upgrade!"
		""
		"The &9Stack Upgrade&r increases the speed of transfer by a stack of items rather than just one. Combine with Speed Upgrades!"
	]
	quest.2B27E4E04A628C60.title: "Speeding Everything Up!"
	quest.2BB884AF43ADC4A6.title: "Need more power?"
	quest.2CCC67629B95C82C.title: "[WIP] Beyond the Valley"
	quest.2E2811D1A0F2A492.quest_desc: [
		"To increase the range of your wireless connection to your system, you'll need to craft &9Range Upgrades&r."
		""
		"The Wireless Transmitter can only hold 4 total. Here's one on the house."
	]
	quest.2E2811D1A0F2A492.title: "Increasing Transmitting Range"
	quest.306FBB49118CCA8D.quest_desc: ["This will prove very useful in servers."]
	quest.30AC00BDC58730C5.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, repairing an item in anvils was made cheaper to help make your tools last longer. This is true with any valid repair material."
		""
		"Unline vanilla, operations like renaming or repairing an item in an anvil do not give any level penalty for next anvil operations."
	]
	quest.30AC00BDC58730C5.title: "Cheap Repair"
	quest.3102F1F1F7ABCAA8.quest_desc: [
		"A basic Brass setup uses 3 Basins in a row, each 1 block apart."
		""
		"The two outer Basins produce Molten Copper and Molten Zinc"
		""
		"Find a way to push both liquids into the center Basin to form Brass."
	]
	quest.3102F1F1F7ABCAA8.title: "Brass Alloy"
	quest.312996060B90E18A.quest_desc: ["On almost all the create contraptions you can hold the \"Ponder\" key on the item and see how they are set up."]
	quest.3134AA1A1DAE3E4D.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, Golden Tools are stronger:"
		""
		"&eIncreased Mining Level&r: Golden Tools can mine up to iron-tier blocks."
		""
		"&eAuto-Repair&r: When in main hand, Golden Tools slowly regain durability over time, making them more viable."
	]
	quest.3134AA1A1DAE3E4D.title: "Golden Tools"
	quest.31469CC0E51402FB.quest_desc: [
		"This pack has Veinmining included."
		""
		"Simply hold the configurable key (\"U\" by default) to harvest multiple blocks simultaneously, streamlining your mining process."
		""
		"Especially useful in early game."
	]
	quest.31469CC0E51402FB.title: "Veinmining"
	quest.326ABA1B37E77C73.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, you can't break logs with bare hands. Try gathering sticks by breaking leaves instead."
		""
		"If you don't have access to trees nearby, you can plant one. Here's a sapling for you!"
	]
	quest.326ABA1B37E77C73.title: "Getting Wood"
	quest.32A81A24A8565209.quest_desc: [
		"The Tool Belt has only 2 slots by default. You can to increase its capacity with a Pouch in an anvil"
		"(up to 9 slots, or 7 upgrades)."
	]
	quest.32CC5131DA8A2CE8.quest_desc: [
		"You can use the Crushing Hammer in the Crafting Table to increase the yield of the raw ores you collected."
		""
		"This helps a lot especially in the early game."
		""
		"Be careful however, as its durability is quite low. Consider repairing it on an Anvil using Copper Ingots, it's much cheaper than crafting a new one."
	]
	quest.34DB6863E6CF1B70.quest_desc: [
		"Allows you to access every part of your RS system."
		""
		"This is the All-In-One Wireless Terminal. It allows you to use the crafting grid, fluid grid, and check on your autocrafting all in one place."
	]
	quest.34DB6863E6CF1B70.title: "Universal Grid"
	quest.34F6CCF469F8BA42.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, block entities like chests, furnaces or spawners can easily be moved, all while keeping their content."
		""
		"Try SHIFT + RIGHT-CLICK on one of you chests with empty hands!"
	]
	quest.34F6CCF469F8BA42.title: "Movable Chests"
	quest.3540A5013B90BF67.quest_desc: [
		"You can use Watterlogged Leaves and Lava to make a &3Cobblestone generator&r."
		""
		"Now you only need to find a way to retreive the products..."
	]
	quest.3540A5013B90BF67.title: "Early Game Automation"
	quest.35637D0BF8CD6E95.title: "Copper Armor"
	quest.3851D000F69C99F0.title: "Molten Zinc"
	quest.39C8833E6BE21817.title: "Hypertube!"
	quest.39FFCAD0284E5F66.title: "Renewable Blaze Cake"
	quest.3AFD7C2C6F4810E0.quest_desc: [
		"The Storage Terminal connects to any kind of inventory or storage and shows you what items are inside."
		""
		"With the help of cables, it can act as a Link between inventories, making a big storage."
	]
	quest.3B089CA14459F118.title: "Piglin in a Box"
	quest.3BDFE13115293F23.title: "Items on the move!"
	quest.4068B736CA930513.title: "Wooden Tools"
	quest.407B628466BD30DA.title: "Copper Tools"
	quest.4103D16FD1FC2B1E.title: "Andesite Machines"
	quest.4310709D0F1539EB.title: "Sticks"
	quest.437C5320DE378471.title: "Electrum Tools"
	quest.43E8912CB307E421.quest_desc: [
		"Great! We can store items virtually, but how do we see what is on the network?"
		""
		"To access the system, you'll need to create a &9Grid&r. The Grid is the most basic form of \"Display\" for the items in your inventory."
	]
	quest.43E8912CB307E421.title: "Accessing Our Network Storage"
	quest.44881E39AB1D62AA.quest_desc: [
		"The &9Crafter&r is where we store recipes for our Network to know how to craft items."
		""
		"These stored recipes are called &9Patterns&r. You can use the Pattern Grid to imprint recipes onto patterns for your network."
		""
		"Once a recipe is placed into the crafter, you'll be able to \"Request\" an item to be crafted from your Grid. You can do this by hitting CTRL+Shift when clicking on the item you have a recipe for to bring up the crafting GUI."
		""
		"This block can also be placed facing a machine to use &9Processing Patterns&r. For example, if you point the Crafter at a Furnace, you can put a recipe inside for a recipe you need a furnace for, like smelting raw processors."
		""
		"As long as the crafter is attached to your system and the Furnace has an importer attached to it, the Crafter will allow you to request the smelted version of the Processor!"
	]
	quest.44881E39AB1D62AA.title: "Automated crafting"
	quest.453F38AA8D11C581.title: "Renewable Fuel"
	quest.4721565D8F4840AB.quest_desc: [
		"This pack uses a &3different food system&r compared to vanilla, making Farmer's Delight's occupy a prime position in your adventure."
		""
		"Here, you have &nthree food slots&r which you must fill with various meals."
		""
		"Eating a food item will fill a slot, giving you the benefits of increased health and regeneration until it runs out."
		""
		"You then cannot eat that food again until the timer runs out (or almost runs out)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"You will start with &nthree hearts&r, and very slow regeneration effect."
		""
		"You must eat food to increase that, up to a maximum of an entire extra bar of hearts if you &neat nutritious meals&r (from Farmer's Delight for example)."
		""
		"Food quality will also impact the regeneration effect, as well as the overall meal duration in the food slot."
		""
		"You can see these stats when you hover over a food item. When you eat it, a timer will appear above your hotbar."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This system ends up balancing many aspects of the game:"
		""
		"- You must &nplan when to eat&r and what foods to eat instead of just chugging bread."
		"- Survival is more difficult, since you don't start with full hearts, and &nmust eat good food&r to build up your durability."
		"- Combat is harder, since &nyou won't regenerate hearts&r until you haven't taken damage in a few seconds (though you can still eat Golden Apples whenever you want)."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"- Farming and cooking is more rewarding, since you can no longer get by with mediocre foods, and &nmust craft good meals&r."
		"- And, lastly, baking cake is actually useful for once, providing a good source of multiple meals that you can quickly eat after respawning."
		""
		"You can also &nreset&r your currently eaten foods by &nvomiting&r, which you can trigger by eating rotten flesh."
	]
	quest.4721565D8F4840AB.title: "Farmer's Delight"
	quest.4CE8193EBC756274.quest_desc: ["Iron Ore is most common around Y level 15."]
	quest.4CE8193EBC756274.title: "Break: 12x Raw Iron"
	quest.4D1FC73EEC60E807.title: "Craftable Totems"
	quest.519BF83279EC0FA0.quest_desc: ["Gravel is abundant in rivers, oceans and hills. You should find some easily."]
	quest.5216C4C9FF433CC6.title: "Electricity"
	quest.522D82D7F29218D2.quest_desc: [
		"You can automate metal production by using the Spout with a Cast underneath to produce ingots, nuggets or blocks (any molten alloy will work)."
		""
		"You can fill up the Spout with any liquid with a &3Mechanical Pump&r or a &3Faucet&r."
	]
	quest.522D82D7F29218D2.title: "Spout"
	quest.53E47DE61A78970B.title: "Diamond Armor"
	quest.547BA1908D596A0E.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, the Golden Armor set is stronger:"
		""
		"&eAuto-Repair&r: When worn, Golden Armor pieces slowly regain durability over time, making the set more viable."
	]
	quest.547BA1908D596A0E.title: "Golden Armor"
	quest.55A06B8657545AF2.title: "Rose Quartz"
	quest.55C8462AEA66561B.quest_desc: ["In this pack, the Dragon Egg can be worn as an accessory and grants special effects to the player."]
	quest.55C8462AEA66561B.title: "An Egg? What for?"
	quest.595EFF9DC26552C5.title: "Brass Machines"
	quest.5AC64D9CE099438E.quest_desc: ["Generates Stress Units when powered with FE."]
	quest.5C16804DAC52F9E5.quest_desc: ["Cook a sophisticated meal to greatly increase your health. Some meals even grant you special effects when consumed."]
	quest.5C16804DAC52F9E5.title: "Nutritious Meals"
	quest.5C40831B7C0CFC40.title: "Steel Tools"
	quest.5CF708FA7A5CE022.quest_desc: ["You can grow crops and saplings faster by spamming Crouch or Sprint around."]
	quest.5CF708FA7A5CE022.title: "Plant Growth"
	quest.5EDD9DC0F1F564E3.quest_desc: [
		"Return Scroll: Lets you return to the waystone you set on the scroll once."
		""
		"Bound Scroll: Bind a waystone to the scroll and when activated, teleports you to it."
		""
		"Warp Scroll: Teleports you to the waystone of your choice."
	]
	quest.5F6AD164007BB533.quest_desc: ["Cut any food or ingredient on a Cutting Board using a Knife."]
	quest.5F6AD164007BB533.title: "Kitchen Work"
	quest.604318155F26ADBA.title: "Dried Kelp"
	quest.613F5D0E5912C52B.quest_desc: ["Try putting an enchanted item and a book into the Grindstone, and see what happens!"]
	quest.613F5D0E5912C52B.title: "Better Grindstone"
	quest.619A9013F288F144.title: "Nethernite Armor"
	quest.62B63D87028259C9.title: "Create: Cheese Factory"
	quest.64D8F5F201AD3E38.quest_desc: ["Wait.. There's more?!"]
	quest.64D8F5F201AD3E38.title: "Going Creative"
	quest.652D1F859CB0EF2A.quest_desc: ["Use the belt to quickely swap your tool without taking space in your hotbar. You can configure the hotkey in the option menu."]
	quest.654FD5D1FD75E50B.title: "Steel Armor"
	quest.65B3A5335F3E19BE.quest_desc: [
		"Used to store FE"
		""
		"Must be built in a 2x2, 3x3, and so on."
	]
	quest.66B8423F31A5930C.title: "Rubber"
	quest.6789A01A055C3CDF.title: "Metal Sheets"
	quest.685EFD90378335E0.title: "Electrum Alloy"
	quest.6904EC449FBEE387.quest_desc: [
		"&9Cables&r are used to connect blocks and items to your system."
		""
		"In the beginning, you can get by with placing blocks next to each other to connect them to your system, but Cables allow you to extend out! This is a staple for any Refined Storage Network."
		""
		"Exporters, Importers and External Storage cables allow you to move items in and out of your system."
	]
	quest.6904EC449FBEE387.title: "Cables"
	quest.6A0BA04368961A62.title: "Iron Tools"
	quest.6AFC0E78A205B2D0.title: "Ingot Casting"
	quest.6B04FC81351CD1AB.quest_desc: [
		"If you want to access your Refined Storage network wirelessly, you'll need to start by creating a &9Wireless Transmitter&r as well as any type of &9Wireless Grid&r."
		""
		"You can attach the Transmitter anywhere on your system. Then, link your Wireless Grid to your system with a right click. You should now be able to access your storage from a distance."
	]
	quest.6D536132DFC006DC.quest_desc: ["Craft or salvage your first Furnace."]
	quest.6FF860AD25032DC8.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, you can use a Recall Potion to instantly travel back to your saved location! Potions for the Nether and End also exist."
		""
		"You can save your location in each dimension by sneak + right-clicking on any valid block."
		""
		"Valid blocks for saving include:"
		"- Overworld: &eCampfire, Bed, Lodestone&r"
		"- Nether: &eSoul Campfire, Respawn Anchor, Lodestone&r"
		"- End : &eLodestone"
	]
	quest.6FF860AD25032DC8.title: "Easy Travel"
	quest.732A1FFD1C2A2889.quest_desc: ["The Sturdy Sheet Block is the only movable block that is as resistant as Obsidian."]
	quest.76C7F2718C532020.quest_desc: [
		"Waystones: Used for teleportation. Most commonly found in villages."
		""
		"Server Waystones:"
		"- Sharestones: Unlike the waystones, they don't need to be activated, and they are always public to everyone."
		"- Portstones: One way Teleportation."
		"Both are very useful for servers."
		""
		"Warp Plates: Two-way teleportation, for you and mobs!"
	]
	quest.77A4A0857722D46B.title: "End Game Gear"
	quest.7978425AF7F46E09.quest_desc: ["The Sturdy Armor is highly durable and offers quite a bit of protection."]
	quest.79B1B4D97101A3FB.quest_desc: ["Lets you teleport to any waystone for free, but has a cooldown."]
	quest.79E403931F26A161.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack, shield's behaviour is slightly altered."
		""
		"When a shield is held in the offhand and not in use, it will not be rendered. Whenever the player right-clicks to raise the shield, it will be shown again, protecting the player vanilla-like. "
		""
		"When not raised in the offhand or when held idle in the main hand, the shield will &3still provide some passive protection&r up to a third of the raised negation."
	]
	quest.7B1FCA37E1EBDC9D.title: "Leather Armor"
	quest.7C4B1A638893B4FE.quest_desc: ["Sturdy Tools have unlimited durability, which makes them very useful when paired with Deployers in your farms."]
	quest.7E757F1FE08369D9.title: "Diamond Tools"
